```asm
; ==============================================================
; PRACTICAL 4
; SUBTRACT Operation on Two User-Entered Numbers
; ==============================================================

; AIM:
; To write an assembly language program that reads two numbers
; A and B from the user and displays the result of A - B.

; THEORY:
; The Basic Computer does not have a direct SUBTRACT instruction.
; Subtraction is performed using 2's complement.
;
; A - B = A + (2's complement of B)
;
; 2's complement of B = B' + 1
;
; CMA -> finds the 1's complement of B
; INC -> adds 1 to obtain the 2's complement of B
; ADD A -> adds A to (-B), giving A - B

; ALGORITHM:
; 1. Read the first number A.
; 2. Store A in memory.
; 3. Read the second number B.
; 4. Find the 1's complement of B using CMA.
; 5. Add 1 using INC to obtain 2's complement of B.
; 6. Add A using ADD A.
; 7. Store the result in DIFF.
; 8. Display the result.
; 9. Halt the program.

; PROGRAM:
; ==============================================================

INP
STA A
INP
CMA
INC
ADD A
STA DIFF
OUT
HLT

A: .data 1 0
DIFF: .data 1 0

; ==============================================================
; TEST CASE:
; A = 18
; B = 50
; A - B = 18 - 50 = -32
;
; RESULT:
; -32
; ==============================================================
